# Lab kit board

The board is the later reference for this project. Update it in the same turn as the work, before the reply.

Board: `/home/matthewh/.cursor/projects/home-matthewh-projects-linux-windows-lab-kit/canvases/lab-kit-kanban.canvas.tsx`

Open list: `/home/matthewh/.cursor/projects/home-matthewh-projects-linux-windows-lab-kit/canvases/next-steps-review.canvas.tsx`

Both files are outside the git repo. Do not commit them.

## When to add a card

Add a card when the user asks for a piece of work, or when an agreed change is large enough to look up later. Skip questions, discussion, and tiny fixes.

Use the next free id in that area (`UI-07`, `GA-08`, `P3-VM-05`). Set `column` to `next` when it is the current job, `backlog` when it is deferred, and `doing` once work starts. One-line `summary`. `detail` says what was asked.

Do not add a second card for work that already has one. Move that card.

## When work finishes

Set that card's `column` to `done`. Rewrite `summary` and `detail` to what actually landed: behavior, the setting or path involved, and anything still unfinished. Do not leave the original request text on a finished card.

A new card id picks up its `column` from `TASKS`. Moving an existing card does not, because `useCanvasState("task-status-v5")` overrides `Task.column`. After any column change, bump that key (`task-status-v6`, then v7, and so on) so the saved column does not hide the update.

If the open set changed, rewrite the "Still open" callout and replace the table in the open-list canvas so it lists only cards that are not done.

Mention the board link when you add or finish a card.
